From 83dcf0303f292eca9c88609a204ccc88b3a31015 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ElixirOffice contributors <noreply@elixiroffice.org>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 17:12:37 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] feat(word): character borders are kept and drawn

A run's border, w:bdr, now has a place in the text properties: read
from and written to the binary format as run property 57 (core 0201),
copied, merged and compared with the rest, kept in the change log, and
drawn as one box around adjacent runs whose borders are equal, with its
left edge where the stretch starts and its right edge where it ends,
across lines. The change log's text properties had no flag bit left:
the border follows the ligatures byte, marked in two of its bits that
older data never sets, so older data reads as before.

From ElixirOffice's sdkjs, commit 3d55711 (their 0.7.0), the part of it
that keeps and draws character borders, with its QUnit test.
